  "summary": "I added a \"Lights off\" button below the canvas, created from `src/main.ts`. Clicking it eases the room to a dim, bluish night look and relabels the button \"Lights on\". Clicking again restores the warm lighting. `typecheck` passes, but I haven't run it in a browser, so I haven't seen the night look or tried the button.\n\nAt night the key light, fill light and hemisphere light drop and shift cool, and the background goes near-black. The dial face gets an emissive glow so it stays readable.\n\n`window.__TASK_STATE__ = { lightsOn, pendulumAngleDeg }` is updated every frame and on each click. `lightsOn` flips as soon as you click. The lighting fades over a few frames. `pendulumAngleDeg` is the pendulum's signed angle from vertical in degrees, with a maximum of about ±12.6° (the 0.22 rad amplitude). A positive value means the bob is swinging toward screen-left."
